;	INTERFACE.  LOCAL MODULES IMPINT, IMPSER, AND NETCON
;	ARE ADDED TO THE MONITOR WITH THIS EDIT.  MONGEN.MAC
;	AND FGEN.HLP HAVE BEEN MODIFIED TO DEFINE ADDITIONAL
;	HDWCNF PARAMETERS AND FEATURE TEST SWITCHES.

;(111)	08-APR-77, JIM MCCOOL
;	MODULES AFFECTED: CLOCK1,COMCON,COMMON,F,S,SCNSER,UUOCON
;	EDIT TYPE: ENHANCEMENT
;	ADD RUTGERS TTY LINKING CODE TO THE MONITOR.  LOCAL
;	MODULE LNKSER IS ADDED TO THE MONITOR WITH THIS EDIT.
;	FGEN.HLP HAS BEEN MODIFIED TO DEFINE FEATURE TEST
;	SWITCH FTLINK.

;(115)	13-MAY-77, DALE STIMSON
;	MODULES AFFECTED: COMLCL,COMMON,S
;	EDIT TYPE: CHANGE
;	TYPICAL REAL-TIME AVIONICS SIMULATIONS AT AFAL DEMAND SUCH
;	A LARGE AMOUNT OF CPU TIME THAT MORE THAN ONE SUCH SIMULATION
;	CANNOT RUN ON THE SAME CPU SIMULTANEOUSLY.  THIS EDIT LIMITS
;	THE NUMBER OF REAL-TIME SIMULATIONS PER CPU TO 1.  INSTALLED
;	UNDER IFN FT.RTL CONDITIONAL.

;(143)	25-MAR-78, DALE STIMSON
;	MODULES AFFECTED:  S, COMMON, COMLCL
;	EDIT TYPE:  ENHANCEMENT
;	ADD SUPPORT FOR IPB INTER-PROCESSOR BUFFER FOR INTERRUPTING
;	BETWEEN CPU'S FOR REAL-TIME SIMULATION.

;(160)	13-JUN-78, JIM MCCOOL
;	MODULES EFFECTED: COMMON
;	EDIT TYPE: ENHANCEMENT
;	ADD THE PATH COMMAND TO RUN THE PATH PROGRAM TO ALLOW
;	USERS TO MORE EASILY CHANGE THEIR DEFAULT PATHS

;(210)	16-OCT-79,	Nick Eastridge
;	EDIT TYPE:	Enhancement
;	MODULES AFFECTED:	COMMON
;	Added the 'PUSH' and 'POP' commands which run PATH
;	to push or pop SFDs from the bottom of the current path.
;	A continuation of edit 160.

;(223)	11-Sep-80, Jim McCool
;	Modules effected: COMCON
;	Edit type: Enhancement
;	Add DOCUMENT command which runs the DOCUMENT program.
;	The DOCUMENT program is similar to the HELP program
;	but reports on .DOC and .MAN files in the DOC: area

;(227)	28-Oct-80, Jim McCool
;	Modules affected: COMMON
;	Add the FINE command as a CCL command to run the FINE editor

;(233)	2-jan-81, provan
;	edit type: expansion
;	modules affected: F, Common, OncMod, Filio
;	description: add code for security monitor.  all code under
;		feature switch FtSecret.  if this switch is off, the
;		monitor has nothing to do with security.  if on, the
;		monitor deals with security problems appropriately
;		for the security level of the monitor running.  the
;		security level for the current monitor is SecLvl, which
;		is unclassified (0) by default, but may be defined as
